<title>TURKEY: Turk Garanti Bank '96 profits up 117 pct.</title>
<headline>Turk Garanti Bank '96 profits up 117 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-Dec 1996 final</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)	1,087.41  vs   1,128.70</p>
<p>    Net profit			19,573.44  vs   9,029.60</p>
<p>    Net interest income	   41,632.27  vs  20,733.59</p>
<p>    Net non-interest expense    19,010.81  vs  10,942.15</p>
<p>    Provisions for bad loans	 774.60  vs     554.80</p>
<p>    Loans			    206,019.72  vs  71,957.17</p>
<p>    Deposits			 194,573.86  vs  85,445.60</p>
<p>    Loans borrowed		 111,170.30  vs  38,908.15</p>
<p>    Equity			    29,156.26  vs  14,079.69</p>
<p>    Capital			   18,000.00  vs   8,000.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Turkiye Garanti Bankasi A.S., a leading Turkish commercial bank, is largely owned by financial and commercial group Dogus.</p>
<p>Figures above do not take into account Turkey's 84.9 percent 1996 wholesale inflation.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875.</p>
</text>
